            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary angioplasty in diabetic patients. Analysis of the problems to improve results].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1637-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The object of this review is to update our knowledge of the results of revascularisation by angioplasty in diabetics. The authors discuss: 1. the clinical results in diabetic patients compared with non-diabetics and the results of coronary bypass surgery; 2. the factors influencing the prognosis of these patients after balloon angioplasty, especially with respect to restenosis; 3. the possibilities of improving the results by the use of modern techniques of revascularisation and prevention and 4. the strategies of revascularisation which may be proposed, based on available data.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
